Decision guide

  concurrent key-value with atomic compounds     -> ConcurrentHashMap
  concurrent set (unordered, fast)               -> ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet()
  concurrent sorted map / set                    -> ConcurrentSkipListMap / Set
  many reads, few writes, snapshot iteration     -> CopyOnWriteArrayList
  producer-consumer with backpressure            -> ArrayBlockingQueue
  direct handoff between threads                 -> SynchronousQueue
  priority ordering of tasks                     -> PriorityBlockingQueue
  delayed/scheduled work                         -> DelayQueue
  non-blocking queue (event loops)               -> ConcurrentLinkedQueue

ForkJoinPool work-stealing

  Worker 1 deque: [T1, T2, T3]    <- owner takes from head (T1)
  Worker 2 deque: [T4]            <- idle -> steals from tail of W1 (T3)
  Worker 3 deque: []              <- idle -> steals from tail of W1 (T2)

  Join: if the joining worker has nothing to do, it steals
        instead of blocking

RecursiveTask (parallel sum)

  class SumTask extends RecursiveTask<Long> {
      private static final int THRESHOLD = 10_000;
      private final long[] arr; private final int lo, hi;
      SumTask(long[] a, int lo, int hi) { this.arr = a; this.lo = lo; this.hi = hi; }
      protected Long compute() {
          if (hi - lo <= THRESHOLD) {
              long sum = 0;
              for (int i = lo; i < hi; i++) sum += arr[i];
              return sum;
          }
          int mid = (lo + hi) >>> 1;
          SumTask left = new SumTask(arr, lo, mid);
          SumTask right = new SumTask(arr, mid, hi);
          left.fork();
          long rightResult = right.compute();  // compute inline
          long leftResult  = left.join();
          return leftResult + rightResult;
      }
  }

  long total = ForkJoinPool.commonPool().invoke(new SumTask(arr, 0, arr.length));

