Bucket pattern -- sensor readings

  // BAD: unbounded array
  { sensorId: 1, readings: [ ... millions ... ] }   // hits 16 MB

  // GOOD: one document per sensor per hour
  {
    sensorId: 1,
    hour: ISODate("2026-01-15T14:00:00Z"),
    readings: [ { t: ..., v: 21.4 }, ... ]          // ~3600 entries max
  }

Decision checklist

  Embed if ALL of:
    - read together most of the time
    - containment (parent owns child)
    - child not queried independently
    - child count bounded / small
    - updates are rare or atomic with parent

  Reference if ANY of:
    - unbounded growth (comments, events, logs)
    - child updated independently
    - child queried/paginated on its own
    - parent would approach 16 MB
    - many-to-many relationship

