 // Resolver tree for { user(id:42) { name orders { total } } }
 // user(42)         -> QueryResolver.user
 // name             -> default resolver on User
 // orders           -> UserResolver.orders
 // total (each)     -> default resolver on Order

 // Four arguments every resolver receives
 // parent  - object returned by parent resolver (root value for top-level)
 // args    - field arguments, already schema-validated
 // context - shared per-request object (auth, loaders, trace id)
 // info    - metadata: field name, parent type, selections, AST

Query:  { orders { id  user { name } } }   (100 orders, 5 distinct users)

Naive execution

  orders resolver      -> SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 100        (1 query)
  user resolver (x100) -> SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?     (100 queries)
  total: 101 queries

With DataLoader

  orders resolver      -> SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 100        (1 query)
  user resolver (x100) -> queues ids [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, ...] and returns futures
                       -> at tick end, one batch fires:
                          SELECT * FROM users WHERE id IN (1, 3, 4, 5, ...)
                       -> 5 distinct ids, 1 query                   (1 query)
  total: 2 queries

DataLoader mechanics

  1. resolver calls loader.load(id)
  2. loader enqueues the id, returns CompletableFuture<User>
  3. engine schedules batch for end of current tick
  4. batch fires with all queued ids (deduplicated)
  5. batch function returns List<User> IN THE SAME ORDER AS INPUT
  6. loader completes each future with the corresponding user

Batch function -- correct shape

  BatchLoader<Long, User> loader = ids -> {
      List<User> users = userRepo.findAllById(ids);           // one query
      Map<Long, User> byId = users.stream()
          .collect(toMap(User::getId, u -> u));
      return ids.stream()                                    // preserve order!
          .map(byId::get)
          .collect(toList());
  };

Per-request DataLoader

  // in the GraphQL context factory (called once per request)
  DataLoaderRegistry registry = new DataLoaderRegistry();
  registry.register("userLoader",
      DataLoaderFactory.newDataLoader(loader, options()));
  context.put("loaders", registry);

  // in a resolver
  DataLoader<Long, User> loader = env.getDataLoader("userLoader");
  return loader.load(parent.getUserId());   // returns CompletableFuture

Spring GraphQL -- declarative

  @BatchMapping
  public Map<User, List<Order>> orders(List<User> users) {
      // one query for all users' orders
      return orderService.byUsers(users);
  }

Common bugs

  - batch returns unordered results -> futures mapped to wrong rows
  - loader created per-call (not per-request) -> no batching, N+1 returns
  - loader is a singleton with a global cache -> cross-user data leaks
  - some resolvers bypass the loader -> N+1 in one branch still hurts

